          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Boba Protein Powder: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            The best boba protein powder for most buyers is <strong>Boba Tea Protein Classic Milk Tea</strong>: 25 g of grass-fed whey isolate, under 1 g of sugar, real black tea, monk fruit as the only sweetener, and about $2.40 per 25 g of protein at the Amazon price we saw on 21 November 2026. Its Taro flavor costs the same and has no caffeine. For a vegan brown sugar milk tea, buy Lunar Lifts; for Thai tea, Tuk Tuk Go.
          </p>

          <p>
            "Boba protein powder" means two things in search. It is the general name for milk-tea-flavored protein, and it is also close to the name of the biggest brand in the niche, Boba Tea Protein, plus a smaller company called Boba Nutrition. We cover both meanings below. None of these powders contains actual tapioca pearls; you add those yourself.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
